# Testing

## Runner

Use `bun:test` — `describe`, `test`, `expect`. Not Jest or Vitest.

## Conventions

- Co-locate test files: `foo.test.ts` next to `foo.ts`.
- Describe blocks group by function/component. Test names start with a verb: `test('returns 404 when spec not found')`.
- AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert — separated by blank lines.
- One assertion per behavior. Multiple `expect` calls are fine if they assert the same behavior.

## Component Tests

Use `@testing-library/react`: `render`, `screen`, `userEvent`. Query by role/label, not class names.

```typescript
import { describe, test, expect } from 'bun:test';
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import { SpecCard } from './SpecCard.js';

describe('SpecCard', () => {
  test('renders the spec title', () => {
    render(<SpecCard title="Auth Flow" status="draft" onSelect={() => {}} />);
    expect(screen.getByText('Auth Flow')).toBeTruthy();
  });
});
```

## Test Fixtures

- Factories live in `__fixtures__/` directories co-located with the module.
- Export builder functions: `createMockSpec()`, `createMockUser()`.

## Mocking

- Mock only external boundaries: HTTP, database, file system.
- Use dependency injection to swap implementations — no mocking libraries.
- NestJS tests: `Test.createTestingModule().overrideProvider().useValue()`.

## E2E

- Playwright for end-to-end tests in `client/ui/e2e/`.
